---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { LINKS } from '../components/siteConfig';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="ExNulla — Applied AI Systems Engineer"
  description="Applied AI systems, governed agent workflows, and production engineering proof."
  active=""
>
  <div class="kicker">James Huson · Applied AI Systems Engineer</div>
  <h1 class="h1">I build AI systems that teams can trust in production.</h1>

  <p class="sub">
    I design and ship auditable agent systems, governed tool execution, deterministic workflows, and
    delivery infrastructure. ExNulla is the working proof: architecture, code, deployment, and
    runnable artifacts in one place.
  </p>

  <div class="btnrow">
    <a class="btn primary" href="/cv">View CV</a>
    <a class="btn ghost" href="/projects">Case Studies</a>
    <a class="btn ghost" href="/lab">Run the Lab</a>
    <a class="btn ghost" href={LINKS.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>
  </div>

  <div class="hr"></div>

  <section class="grid grid-2">
    <div>
      <h2>What I build</h2>
      <p>
        AI features become useful when they are connected to real workflows and bounded by clear
        contracts. I build the layer around the model: schemas, tools, state, validation, security,
        observability, and deployment.
      </p>
      <p>
        My work sits between applied AI engineering, platform architecture, and operational
        delivery: turning uncertain model output into inspectable systems that can be tested,
        operated, and improved.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2>What you will find here</h2>
      <ul class="list">
        <li>
          <strong>Case studies:</strong> real constraints, architecture decisions, and shipped proof.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>CV:</strong> the skills, systems, and role fit behind the work.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Lab:</strong> sandboxed demos where the ideas stop being theory.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Engineering:</strong> the design and delivery practices behind the systems.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="hr"></div>

  <section>
    <h2>How I can help a team</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-3">
      <article class="card">
        <h2 style="font-size:18px; margin:0 0 8px">AI platform design</h2>
        <p class="small" style="margin:0 0 12px">
          Agent orchestration, tool boundaries, RAG/context flows, validation, observability, and
          governance that survive beyond the prototype.
        </p>
        <div class="btnrow">
          <a class="btn ghost" href="/projects">See case studies</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <h2 style="font-size:18px; margin:0 0 8px">Systems delivery</h2>
        <p class="small" style="margin:0 0 12px">
          TypeScript, Node, Python, PostgreSQL, CI/CD, cloud deployment, release discipline, and
          recovery-minded operations.
        </p>
        <div class="btnrow">
          <a class="btn ghost" href="/cv">View experience</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <h2 style="font-size:18px; margin:0 0 8px">Trustworthy AI</h2>
        <p class="small" style="margin:0 0 12px">
          Schema gates, threat modeling, prompt-injection resistance, audit trails, deterministic
          fallbacks, and human accountability around model output.
        </p>
        <div class="btnrow">
          <a class="btn ghost" href="/lab">Open Lab</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="hr"></div>

  <section class="card">
    <div class="kicker">Featured case</div>
    <h2 style="margin-top:4px">Nexus — Governed AI Action Runtime</h2>
    <p>
      A TypeScript/Node runtime that keeps AI-assisted actions behind schemas, authority boundaries,
      deterministic gates, audit records, threat tests, and CI enforcement.
    </p>
    <p class="small">
      This is the kind of work I want to be known for: making AI useful without making it
      unaccountable.
    </p>
    <div class="btnrow">
      <a
        class="btn ghost"
        href="https://github.com/Thesis-Web/nexus"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer">Open GitHub</a
      >
      <a class="btn ghost" href="/projects/attest-pipeline">View related case study</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="hr"></div>

  <section class="grid grid-2">
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Built end to end</h2>
      <p class="small" style="margin:0 0 12px">
        ExNulla is a working reference implementation of how I operate: define the problem, lock the
        constraints, build the smallest useful system, verify it, deploy it, and document the
        trade-offs.
      </p>
      <ul class="list">
        <li>Architecture, implementation, deployment, and operations in one loop.</li>
        <li>Static-first shell with atomic releases and sandboxed demo windows.</li>
        <li>Public source and runnable proof wherever confidentiality allows.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2>Operating stance</h2>
      <ul class="list">
        <li>Start with limits, not features.</li>
        <li>Prefer systems that are inspectable, testable, and cheap to recover.</li>
        <li>Use AI aggressively, but keep judgment and accountability human.</li>
        <li>Move fast where ambiguity is low; slow down where the architecture matters.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="small" style="margin-top:12px">
        The goal is simple: make the work legible to the people hiring for applied AI, platform, and
        systems delivery.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="hr"></div>

  <section class="identity">
    <div class="identity-inner">
      <img src="/assets/James-Headshot.jpg" alt="James Huson" loading="lazy" />
      <div>
        <strong>James Huson</strong>
        <div class="small">Developer architecture, systems thinking, and public proof-of-work.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="btnrow" style="justify-content:center;">
      <a class="btn ghost" href={LINKS.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="https://github.com/Thesis-Web" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"
        >GitHub</a
      >
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .identity {
      display: grid;
      gap: 18px;
      justify-items: center;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .identity-inner {
      display: grid;
      gap: 14px;
      justify-items: center;
      width: 100%;
    }

    .identity-inner img {
      width: min(100%, 360px);
      aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
      object-fit: cover;
      object-position: center top;
      border-radius: 18px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      display: block;
    }

    @media (max-width: 640px) {
      .identity-inner img {
        width: min(100%, 300px);
      }

      .identity .btnrow {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
        gap: 10px;
        width: 100%;
        justify-content: stretch !important;
      }

      .identity .btnrow .btn {
        width: 100%;
      }

      .identity .btnrow .btn:last-child {
        grid-column: 1 / -1;
      }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
